-- title:
--   Admissible residues are integral over κ_A[jmath̄]
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5\le q$ and a nonzero level $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$, and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ from the field $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(X(M'))$ — the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$ — to the field $\kappa_A(j,j_{M'})$ generated over the residue field $\kappa_A$ of $A$ by `jqModC` and `jqNModC` inside Laurent series over $\kappa_A$; thus $R_0$ comes with a valuation subring of integers, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and orders, and compatibility with $A$. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(X(M'))$ is $R_0$-integral, with residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $\mathcal A$ be a subring of $\mathbb Q$-Laurent series whose elements are exactly the $gf$ lying in the full level-$M'$ modular function field, $R_0$-integral after coefficient extension to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and cusp-regular with respect to $j$, i.e. $\operatorname{ord}_P(gf)\ge 0$ at every place $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(X(M'))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\operatorname{ord}_P(j)\ge 0$; assume $j\in\mathcal A$. The conclusion: for every such $gf$ in the full modular function field that is $R_0$-integral and lies in $\mathcal A$, and given $R_0$-integrality of $j$, the residue $R_0(\overline{gf})$ is integral over the $\kappa_A$-subalgebra of $\kappa_A(j,j_{M'})$ generated by the residue of $j$. The proof uses neither the hypothesis $5\le q$ nor the hypothesis $j\in\mathcal A$.
--
--   This is the integrality step for the reduction of the full level-$M'$ modular function field: residues of admissible rational functions are integral over $\kappa_A[\bar\jmath]$, the classical statement that a function regular at all places where $j$ is regular is integral over the $j$-line. It is used in the construction of an algebra homomorphism from the level-$M'$ function field in characteristic $q$ out of a ring homomorphism on admissible functions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isIntegral_adjoin_residue_jq_residue_of_mem_admissible.lean

